# App wiki help — shell Help menu & AI corpus

Child apps expose **markdown help** at **`/wiki/`** on their public origin (`https://{module_code}.apps.vtc.com`). The VTC shell **Help** item in the app chrome dropdown loads this content — not from the shell repo.

## Shell loader (reference)

`~/apps/app/src/lib/features/apps/app-help/fetch-app-wiki-help.ts`:

1. **ZAPI** — `GET /api/v1/ai/apps/{moduleCode}/wiki` (when published)
2. **Static wiki** — `{appOrigin}/wiki/index.json` then each listed `.md` page
3. **Fallback probes** (single page each): `help.md`, `{moduleCode}.md`, `apps/{moduleCode}.md`, `README.md`

`appOrigin` comes from the app's **`module_url`** / launch URL in the catalog (e.g. `https://leads400dm.apps.vtc.com`).

## Required files (every child app)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `public/wiki/help.md` | Primary help article (H1 title used in UI) |
| `public/wiki/index.json` | Manifest listing wiki pages |

### `index.json` shape

```json
{
  "pages": [
    { "path": "help.md", "title": "My App — Help" }
  ]
}
```

- **`path`** — filename under `/wiki/` (must end in `.md`)
- **`title`** — optional; shell uses first `# Heading` in the markdown when omitted

### Vite static apps

Files live in **`public/wiki/`** — Vite copies them to `dist/wiki/` on build. No extra config.

### Next.js apps

Files live in **`public/wiki/`** — served at `/wiki/*` by Next static file handler.

## Platform wiki (shell AI corpus)

The **main shell** also maintains platform help at `~/apps/app/public/wiki/` for Vault AI / AI Guide ingestion — see `~/apps/app/helpdocs/INGESTION.md`.

| Location | Audience |
|----------|----------|
| `{child}/public/wiki/` | **In-app Help** menu when that app is open |
| `~/apps/app/public/wiki/apps/{module_code}.md` | Platform catalog / Guide corpus (optional but recommended) |

Do not confuse the two: child `help.md` is fetched cross-origin from the app URL; shell `public/wiki/apps/*.md` is for platform-wide support docs.

## Checklist (new or migrated app)

1. Add `public/wiki/help.md` with H1 title and sections: opening the app, main workflow, space scoping, support.
2. Add `public/wiki/index.json` listing at least `help.md`.
3. Optionally add `~/apps/app/public/wiki/apps/{module_code}.md` for platform Guide.
4. **Verify after deploy:** `curl -s https://{module_code}.apps.vtc.com/wiki/index.json` and `.../wiki/help.md`.
5. Open app in shell → **⋯** → **Help** — page should render (not "no help available").

## Static deploy note

Apps on the **static lane** (`runtime_type=static`) must **not** remain on a publisher Next.js shard ingress. They are listed in build `excludeModules` and served via `static-apps-gateway`. If Help or the app itself 503s, check for a conflicting `app-runtime-publisher-shard-*` ingress host rule.

